description:
///NEEC INCIDENT NOTIFICATION: CITIZEN COMPLAINT | POSSIBLE LEAK FROM PIPELINE UNDERWATER | LAKE ERIE | PORT MAITLAND, ON ///

CALLER EXPLAINS ENBRIDGE DISPATCH THAT HE WAS SAILING AND PASSED BY AN AREA THAT WAS BUBBLING OUT NOTICED A ROTTEN EGG SULPHUR SMALL.
ENBRIDGE VERIFIED THAT THEY DO NOT HAVE NAY GAS LINES IN THE LOCATION.

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1465570///

UPDATED INFORMATION: CALLER REPORTED THAT AFTER FURTHER INVESTIGATION, THE INCIDENT DOES NOT MEET THE RQ

ORIGINAL INFORMATION: CALLER IS REPORTING A RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF NATURAL GAS INTO THE ATMOSPHERE FROM A GATHERING PIPELINE. CAUSE OF RELEASE IS UNKNOWN. INVESTIGATION IS ONGOING. CALLER HAD NO FURTHER INFORMATION.

/// THIS IS A 48 HOUR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1465587 ///

THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE IS DUE TO INTERNAL CORROSION. THIS UPDATES THE INCIDENT CAUSE TO EQUIPMENT FAILURE.

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

THE CALLER IS REPORTING A RELEASE OF LIQUID CONDENSATE, ONTO THE GROUND,  FROM A 6" STEEL NATURAL GAS GATHERING PIPELINE. THE CALLER STATES THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE IS UNKNOWN.

/// THIS IS A 48 HOUR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1465466 ///

THE RELEASE HAS BEEN SECURED AND REPAIRS ARE UNDERWAY.

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

CALLER REPORTING THE RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF ETHANE FROM A PIPELINE DUE TO A VALVE MALFUNCTION.

/// THIS IS A DRILL ///


CALLER STATES THAT WHILE TRANSFERRING 'BROWN EDIBLE OIL' FROM A STORAGE TANK TO A TANK BARGE, THE 8" STEEL TRANSFER PIPE RUPTURED, DISCHARGING 24.66 BARRELS INTO THE MISSISSIPPI RIVER.


/// THIS IS A DRILL ///

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1465415 ///

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE AMOUNT OF MATERIAL THAT RELEASED IS BEING UPDATED TO (29.4) TONS. THE PRODUCT THAT RELEASED IS BEING CHANGED FROM IRON ORE TO LEAD ORE.  THE LOCATION IS BEING UPDATED AS WELL. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

THE CALLER STATED THAT A TRACTOR TRAILER TRUCK AND SIDE DUMP TRAILER OVERTURNED AT THE LOCATION. THE CAUSE OF THE INCIDENT IS BEING ATTRIBUTED TO ANOTHER VEHICLE RUNNING THE TRUCK OFF THE ROAD WHILE TAKING A SHARP TURN. BECAUSE OF THIS (15) TONS OF IRON ORE RELEASED ONTO THE ROAD.

/// THIS IS A POTENTIAL RELEASE ///


CALLER STATES THEY RECEIVED A REPORT THAT A VESSEL SANK IN THE HARBOR FOR UNKNOWN REASONS.

ALTHOUGH NO SHEEN HAS BEEN OBSERVED, IT IS ESTIMATED THAT APPROX 50 GALLONS OF DIESEL AND/OR OIL IS CURRENTLY ON BOARD THE VESSEL.


/// THIS IS A POTENTIAL RELEASE ///

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1465429 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THE AMOUNT OF ANHYDROUS AMMONIA RELEASED WAS DETERMINED TO BE 5 POUNDS. THE SOURCE OF THE RELEASE WAS DETERMINED TO BE A LOOSE BOLT ON A FLANGE.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER IS REPORTING A RELEASE OF ANHYDROUS AMMONIA, INTO THE  ATMOSPHERE, FROM REFRIGERATION PIPING INSIDE THE FACILITY. THE CALLER  STATES THE CAUSE  OF THE RELEASE IS UNKNOWN AT THIS TIME.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1465429 ///

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1465301 /// 

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT ONLY (40) GALLONS OF MATERIAL RELEASED DURING THE COURSE OF THIS INCIDENT. THE CALLER DISCOVERED SRP INFORMATION WHICH WILL BE UPDATED IN THIS REPORT. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 


THE CALLER STATED THAT A NURSE TANK RELEASED (750) GALLONS OF AMMONIA INTO  THE ATMOSPHERE. THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE IS CURRENTLY UNKNOWN. THE INCIDENT OCCURRED WHEN THE TANK WAS BEING PICKED UP. ALTHOUGH THE CAUSE OF THE  RELEASE IS UNKNOWN THE CALLER SUSPECTS AN UNSPECIFIED MAINTENANCE ISSUE  WITH THE TANKS VALVE.

/// THIS IS A UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1465352 ///

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT THEY DISCOVERED THAT ONLY (25) GALLONS OF MATERIAL RELEASED DURING THE COURSE OF THIS INCIDENT. THE CALLER STATED THAT THIS IS BELOW THE RQ. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///  

THE CALLER STATES A D9 BULLDOZER HAD A RUPTURED LINE, WHICH RESULTED IN A  RELEASE OF (55) GALLONS OF HYDRAULIC OIL IMPACTED THE GROUND.

/// THIS IS A 48 HOUR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1465306 ///

THE CALLER UPDATED THE RELEASE AMOUNT TO 1000 MCF. THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE WAS DUE TO OPERATOR ERROR AFTER THE LINE WAS STRUCK DURING BORING OPERATIONS. THE RELEASE HAS BEEN SECURED. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

CALLER REPORTING THE DISCHARGE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF NATURAL GAS, FROM  THE CRAWFORD #1 PIPELINE, A CLASS 3 TRANSMISSION PIPELINE. THE MATERIAL IS  DISCHARGING TO THE AIR DUE TO THE LINE BEING STRUCK DURING BORING  OPERATIONS. THE PRECISE CAUSE AND AMOUNT ARE UNDER INVESTIGATION.

/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///


CALLER STATES THERE IS AN UNKNOWN VESSEL AT THE 'LANDS END MOTEL', TAKING ON WATER, WITH A POTENTIAL TO RELEASE AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF UNKNOWN OIL TO THE SAYVILLE FERRY CAHHNEL

CALLER HAD VERY LIMITED INFORMATION; VESSEL IS NOT KNOWN TO BE SINKING AT THIS TIME.


/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///

////NEEC INCIDENT NOTIFICATION: SUNKEN JET SKI | DETROIT RIVER | WINDSOR, ON////
RISK OF POLLUTION
DESCRIPTION: 2026/06/13 22:18 SUNKEN PWC WAS REPORTED TO JRCC TRENTON. POB WERE CONFIRMED SAFE ON SHORE. NO SAR CASE OR FURTHER INFORMATION AVAILABLE FROM JRCC TRENTON. CONTACT WINDSOR POLICE WITH THE INCIDENT NUMBER FOR MORE INFORMATION.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1465156 /// 

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT THEY RECEIVED THEIR SAMPLES, WHICH CONFIRMED NO PCB’S WERE PRESENT. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///  


	CALLER STATES THAT A MECHANIC FAILURE OCCURRED ON A BANK OF 2 TRANSFORMERS, CAUSING BOTH TO LEAK AN ESTIMATED COMBINED TOTAL OF 10 GALLONS OF MINERAL  OIL (UNKNOWN IF CONTAINING PCBS) TO ASPHALT AND 3 VEHICLES BELOW.

NO IMPACT TO WATERWAYS.

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1465063///

THE UPDATED INFORMATION IS AS FOLLOWS: 600 POUNDS OF FREON WAS RELEASED.

THE ORIGINAL REPORTED INFORMATION IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER REPORTED A RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF REFRIGERANT FROM REFRIGERANT PIPING AT A WAREHOUSE THAT WENT INTO THE AIR OF THE FACILITY AT THE INCIDENT LOCATION. THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE IS DUE TO A JACK HAMMER HITTING THE LINE DURING CONSTRUCTION.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1465120 ///

THE CALLER UPDATED THE NUMBER OF DERAILED CARS FROM 5 TO 8. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

5 LOADED GRAIN CARS DERAILED WITH NO INJURIES

/// THIS IS ANOTHER UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1465120 ///

THE CALLER UPDATED THE NUMBER OF DERAILED CARS FROM 8 TO 10.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1465120 ///

THE CALLER UPDATED THE NUMBER OF DERAILED CARS FROM 5 TO 8. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

5 LOADED GRAIN CARS DERAILED WITH NO INJURIES

/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///   

THE CALLER REPORTED A MOORED 24FT WORK VESSEL IS CAPSIZED IN ALA WAI HARBOR AT THE INCIDENT LOCATION. THE CAUSE OF THE VESSEL BECOMING CAPSIZED IS UNKNOWN. 

-IT IS UNKNOWN IF THERE ARE ANY OILS / FUELS ON BOARD.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464899 ///

/// THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS ///

THE CALLER UPDATED THE RELEASE AMOUNT TO 247 POUNDS. THE RELEASE HAS BEEN SECURED. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

CALLER REPORTED THE RELEASE OF MATERIALS FROM A FAULTY VALVE. THERE ARE NO  OFFSITE IMPACTS OR EVACUATIONS AT THIS TIME.

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464819///

THE UPDATED INFORMATION IS AS FOLLOWS: THE SUSPECTED RESPONSIBLE PARTY (SRP) HAS BEEN UPDATED.

ORIGINAL REPORTED INFORMATION: THE CALLER REPORTED THAT DURING A BILGE SLOP TRANSFER FROM A CONTAINER VESSEL TO A DOCKSIDE TANKER TRUCK, THE TANKER TRUCK "BURPED" DUE TO UNKNOWN REASONS. THIS RESULTED IN THE RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF BILGE SLOPS ONTO THE DOCK, AND INTO THE WATERS OF THE OAKLAND INNER HARBOR. THE CALLER DID NOT KNOW IF A SHEEN WAS CREATED ON THE WATER.

/// THIS IS A 48 HOUR PHMSA UPDATE ///

BECAUSE THIS IS A REQUIRED 48 HOUR UPDATE, THE INCIDENT TYPE HAS BEEN CHANGED TO PIPELINE. THE CALLER ALSO UPDATED THE RELEASE AMOUNT TO 10.421 MMCF. THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE HAS BEEN UPDATED TO EQUIPMENT FAILURE DUE TO A FAULTY VALVE. THE RELEASE DURATION WAS 188 MINUTES. THERE WAS NO ENVIRONMENTAL IMPACT OR MEDIA INTEREST.

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

THE CALLER STATES HEAVY STORMS CAUSED A POWER LOSS AT THE COMPRESSOR  STATION, WHICH CAUSED A GAS RELEASE.

THE CALLER BELIEVES THEY MAY EXCEED THE RQ.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464891 ///

THE CALLER UPDATED THE RELEASE AMOUNT TO 8.4 POUNDS OF AMMONIA. THE DURATION OF THE RELEASE WAS 77 MINUTES.

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

ANHYDROUS AMMONIA RELEASED FROM WITHIN THE ENGINE ROOM OF THE AMMONIA  PROCESSING FACILITY DUE TO AN UNKNOWN CAUSE AT THIS TIME.  CALLER STATES  THERE WAS A HIGH LEVEL ALARM IN THEIR FACILITY (97PPM).

///POTENTIAL RELEASE REPORT///

THE CALLER IS REPORTING A POTENTIAL RELEASE OF GASOLINE, INTO THE DETROIT RIVER, FROM A CAPSIZED PLEASURE CRAFT. THE CALLER STATES THE CAUSE OF THE INCIDENT IS UNKNOWN. CALLER STATES THAT SMALL BOAT STATION BELLE ISLE RESCUED (3) INDIVIDUALS ONBOARD.

CALLER STATES THAT THERE WERE NO INJURIES OR FATALITIES IN THIS INCIDENT.

/// THIS IS A PHMSA 48- HOUR UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464620 /// 

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT (20.5) MCF OF NATURAL GAS RELEASED DURING THIS INCIDENT. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

NATURAL GAS RELEASED FROM A PIPELINE COMPRESSOR DUE TO AN UNKNOWN CAUSE AT  THIS TIME.  CALLER STATES THE COMPRESSOR ALSO CAUGHT ON FIRE.

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464675///

THE UPDATED INFORMATION IS AS FOLLOWS: REPAIRS HAVE BEEN COMPLETED. THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE IS STILL UNKNOWN.

THE ORIGINAL REPORTED INFORMATION IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER DISCOVERED A RELEASE OF NATURAL GAS, INTO THE ATMOSPHERE, FROM A 12" TRANSMISSION PIPELINE. THE CALLER STATES THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE IS UNKNOWN, BUT THEY SUSPECT IT TO BE CORROSION. THE INVESTIGATION IS CURRENTLY UNDERWAY.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464572 /// 

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT THE CONCENTRATION OF THE MATERIAL THAT RELEASED WAS (12.5) PERCENT. THE CALLER ALSO STATED THAT A CONTRACTOR IS ENROUTE TO THE LOCATION FOR REMEDIATION.

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///    

CALLER REPORTING THE RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF SODIUM HYPOCHLORITE,  FROM A FACILITY CHEMICAL LINE, TO THE FACILITY FLOORING AND CONTAINMENT,  WITH APPROX (400) GALLONS ENTERING INTO A STORM DRAIN, DUE TO A LINE  BREAKING FOR AN UNSPECIFIED CAUSE. FURTHER INVESTIGATION IS UNDERWAY.

/// THIS IS A 48-HOUR UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464600 ///

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT NO CHANGES HAVE OCCURRED FOR THIS INCIDENT.  

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

	THE CALLER DISCOVERED AN UNKNOWN SHEEN FROM AN UNKNOWN SOURCE IN THE GULF  OF AMERICA.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1464395 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THE PRODUCT THAT RELEASED WAS DETERMINED TO ACTUALLY BE FUEL OIL, IN THE AMOUNT OF 2 LITERS.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: CALLER REPORTED THAT 1 CUBIC METER OF LUBE OIL RELEASED FROM A LIFE BOAT  ATTACHED TO A BULK CARRIER. THE VESSEL WAS CONDUCTING AN OIL SPILL DRILL,  AND WHEN THEY STARTED THE LIFE BOAT, THEY NOTICED OIL IN THE WATER. CAUSE  OF THE RELEASE IS UNKNOWN. NO SHEEN DETAILS WERE PROVIDED.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1464395 ///

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1464472 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THE STATION WAS BROUGHT BACK ONLINE ON JUNE 6 AT 0503. THE CAUSE OF THE INCIDENT IS STILL UNDETERMINED.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: 	THE CALLER REPORTED A RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF NATURAL GAS FROM A  COMPRESSOR STATION THAT WENT INTO THE AIR AT THE INCIDENT LOCATION. THE  CAUSE OF THE RELEASE IS UNKNOWN AND UNDER INVESTIGATION.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1464472 ///

/// THIS IS A CORRECTION TO NRC REPORT 1464335 ///

THE INCIDENT LOCATION WAS INCORRECTLY LISTED IN THE ORIGINAL REPORT. THIS REPORT PROVIDES THE CORRECT INCIDENT LOCATION. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

CALLER IS REPORTING A VALVE LEAK ON A TRANSMISSION PIPELINE THAT IS  ACTIVELY RELEASING AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF NATURAL GAS INTO THE ATMOSPHERE.  ONSITE CREW TRYING TO SECURE RELEASE. NO OTHER REMEDIAL ACTIONS REPORTED.  NO INJURIES OR EVACUATIONS REPORTED. CALLER HAD NO FURTHER INFORMATION.

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464335///

UPDATE: 1,068.171 MCF OF MATERIAL WAS RELEASED. THE RELEASE HAS BEEN SECURED.

ORIGINAL: CALLER IS REPORTING A VALVE LEAK ON A TRANSMISSION PIPELINE THAT IS ACTIVELY RELEASING AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF NATURAL GAS INTO THE ATMOSPHERE. ONSITE CREW TRYING TO SECURE RELEASE. NO OTHER REMEDIAL ACTIONS REPORTED. NO INJURIES OR EVACUATIONS REPORTED. CALLER HAD NO FURTHER INFORMATION.

/// THIS IS A 48 HOUR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464349 ///

THE CALLER HAS NO MAJOR UPDATES TO PROVIDE.

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

THE CALLER REPORTED THAT THERE IS A PINHOLE LEAK ON THE RECIRCULATION  SYSTEM AT A TANK FARM. THIS RESULTED IN THE RELEASE OF 30 GALLONS OF CRUDE  OIL INTO CONTAINMENT. NO WATERWAYS OR STORM DRAINS WERE AFFECTED.

/// THIS IS A 48 HOUR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464377 /// 

THE CALLER REPORTED THAT THE RELEASE WAS DUE TO A PINHOLE LEAK. THE RELEASE HAS BEEN SECURED. THERE WAS NO ENVIRONMENTAL IMPACT REPORTED.

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

THE CALLER REPORTED A DISCHARGE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF DIESEL FUEL FROM AN UNDERGROUND DISTRIBUTION PIPELINE THAT WENT INTO A STORM SEWER SYSTEM AND  ONTO THE GROUND OF A PARKING LOT / STREET AT THE INCIDENT LOCATION. THE  CAUSE OF THE DISCHARGE IS UNKNOWN AT THIS TIME.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464144 ///

THE CALLER UPDATED THE DATE OF OCCURRENCE TO MAY 27TH.

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

CALLER REPORTED THAT 100 GALLONS OF MOTOR OIL OVERFLOWED FROM AN OIL  SKIMMING PROCESS TANK AT A SEWAGE TREATMENT FACILITY DUE TO HEAVY RAIN.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464204 ////

THE CALLER UPDATED THE RELEASE AMOUNT TO 450 GALLONS. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

MORE THAN 5 GALLONS OF AQUEOUS FILM FORMING FOAM (AFFF) RELEASED FROM A  POLY TANK DUE TO A VALVE BEING LEFT OPEN DURING AN ANNUAL MAINTENANCE  INSPECTION ON THE SYSTEM.

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464131///

UPDATED INFORMATION: TXRR HAS BEEN NOTIFIED. ALL OTHER UNKNOWN DETAILS ARE STILL UNDER INVESTIGATION.

ORIGINAL INFORMATION: CALLER REPORTED A FIRE INVOLVING A NATURAL GAS COMPRESSOR STATION (TYPE-R SYSTEM). IT IS UNKNOWN AT THIS TIME IF ANY NATURAL GAS HAS RELEASED FROM THE COMPRESSOR. THE COST IN DAMAGES WILL BE ABOVE $149,000 BUT THE TOTAL COST IS UNKNOWN.

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464121///

UPDATED INFORMATION: THE AMOUNT OF MATERIAL THAT RELEASED WAS UPDATED TO 58 POUNDS, PREVIOUSLY UNKNOWN. THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE WAS FOUND BE FROM PACKING THAT HAD SHIFTED AND COME LOOSE. RELEASE WAS SECURED AT 0842 ON THE DAY OF THE INCIDENT, AND THE PACKING WAS CORRECTED.

ORIGINAL INFORMATION: CALLER REPORTING THE RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF AMMONIA FROM A VALVE ON THE ROOF OF THEIR PLANT. THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE IS UNKNOWN. RELEASE ONGOING, CALLER STATES THEY DO NOT BELIEVE THE RELEASE HAS REACHED THE RQ.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1464205 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THIS INCIDENT WAS DETERMINED TO BE NON-JURISDICITONAL AND SHOULD NOT HAVE BEEN CALLED IN. INITIAL INFORMATION STATED THAT THE CUSTOMER STRUCK A SERVICE LINE OUTSIDE THEIR HOME, WHICH WAS INCORRECT. IN REALITY, THE CUSTOMER CUT A FUEL LINE IN THEIR OWN BASEMENT.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: 	THE CALLER REPORTED A PRIVATE RESIDENT ACCIDENTALLY CUT THE GAS LINE IN  THEIR YARD. SHORTLY AFTERWARDS, THERE WAS AN EXPLOSION IN THEIR HOME. IT IS UNKNOWN IF THERE WERE ANY FIRES. THIS RESULTED IN THE RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF NATURAL GAS INTO THE ATMOSPHERE.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1464205 ///

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464140///

UPDATED: THE SUSPECTED RESPONSIBLE PARTY HAS BEEN UPDATED TO UNKNOWN. CALLER STATED THAT ALL INVESTIGATIONS INDICATE THE VESSEL DID NOT RELEASE ANY MATERIAL.

ORIGINAL INFORMATION: THE CALLER REPORTED THAT THE MAIN ENGINE ON A FERRY VESSEL HAD A DISCHARGE DUE TO UNKNOWN REASONS. THE CALLER SUSPECTS AN UNKNOWN MECHANICAL FAILURE TO THE GEAR COOLER, BUT THIS IS STILL BEING INVESTIGATED. THIS RESULTED IN THE RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF AN UNKNOWN OIL INTO THE WATERS OF RACCOON STRAIT.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1464016 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THE AMOUNT OF HYDRAULIC OIL RELEASED WAS DETERMINED TO BE 106 GALLONS.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: CALLER REPORTING THE DISCHARGE OF APPROX (20-30) GALLONS OF HYDRAULIC OIL,  FROM A HEAVY TOP LOADER, TO THE LAND/SOIL DUE TO AN UNSPECIFIED MALFUNCTION OF THE HYDRAULIC LINE. NO WATERWAY IMPACT REPORTED.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1464016 ///

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1464011 /// 

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THE TANK HAS EMPTIED, SO RELEASE IS SECURED. THE DURATION OF THE RELEASE WAS 5.2 HOURS, AND THE AMOUNT OF ACETIC ACID RELEASE WAS DETERMINED TO BE 21,316 POUNDS. ADEM WAS ON SITE.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: 
CALLER REPORTED AN ACID TANK DEVELOPED A SIGNIFICANT HOLE THAT CAUSED THE  MATERIALS TO DRAIN INTO THE SEWER AND WASTE WATER OPERATIONS. THERE WILL BE A RELEASE TO THE ATMOSPHERE THAT IS BELIEVED WILL EXCEED THE REPORTING  REQUIREMENTS FOR REPORTING.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1464011 ///

/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///

THE CALLER REPORTED AN UNKNOWN ELECTRONIC DEVICE OVERHEATED DURING A COMMERCIAL FLIGHT FROM SYDNEY, AUSTRALIA TO LAX (LOS ANGELES) AIRPORT FOR UNKNOWN REASONS. THE CALLER STATED THE DEVICE WAS PLACED INSIDE A FIRE CONTAINMENT BAG.

-IT IS UNKNOWN IF THERE WAS ANY RELEASE OF ANY SMOKE.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464044 ////

THE CALLER UPDATED THE RELEASE AMOUNT TO 3547 POUNDS.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1464011 /// 

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THE TANK HAS EMPTIED, SO RELEASE IS SECURED. THE  DURATION OF THE RELEASE WAS 5.2 HOURS, AND THE AMOUNT OF ACETIC ACID  RELEASE WAS DETERMINED TO BE 21,316 POUNDS. ADEM WAS ON SITE.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: 
CALLER REPORTED AN ACID TANK DEVELOPED A SIGNIFICANT HOLE THAT CAUSED THE   MATERIALS TO DRAIN INTO THE SEWER AND WASTE WATER OPERATIONS. THERE WILL BE A RELEASE TO THE ATMOSPHERE THAT IS BELIEVED WILL EXCEED THE REPORTING   REQUIREMENTS FOR REPORTING.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464053 /// 

THE CALLER UPDATED THE RELEASE AMOUNTS TO 62.32 POUNDS OF BENZENE, 15,665.72 POUNDS OF METHANE, 3,133.34 POUNDS OF VOLATILE ORGANIC COMPOUNDS (VOCS), 83.57 POUNDS OF TOLUENE, 2.44 POUNDS OF ETHYL BENZENE, 42.5 POUNDS OF XYLENE

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

THE CALLER IS REPORTING A RELEASE OF BENZENE AND METHANE, TO THE  ATMOSPHERE, FROM BOTH THERMAL OXIDIZER UNIT AT THE FACILITY. THE CALLER  STATES THAT BOTH THERMAL OXIDIZER UNITS TRIPPED.

/// THIS IS A 48 HOUR UPDATE TO REPORT 1463947 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THE AMOUNT OF REFRIGERANT RELEASED WAS DETERMINED TO BE 50 POUNDS, THE EQUIVALENT OF ABOUT 10 GALLONS. NO REPORTABLE QUANTITIES WERE EXCEEDED.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: 
CALLER REPORTING THE RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF MIXED REFRIGERANT FROM A TRAIN 1 CHILLER TO THE AIR/ATMOSPHERE WITH A 'SMALL' AMOUNT RELEASING TO  CONCRETE. THE PRECISE CAUSE AND AMOUNT ARE UNDER INVESTIGATION.

/// THIS IS A 48 HOUR UPDATE TO REPORT 1463947 ///

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1464002 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THE AMOUNT OF PYGAS RELEASED IS NOW ESTIMATED TO BE 400 GALLONS.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: 	"PYGAS" RELEASED FROM A VACUUM BREAKER ON THE ROOF OF TANK 1701 DUE TO AN  EQUIPMENT FAILURE.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1464002 ///

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1463980 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THE SEWAGE RELEASE BEGAN AGAIN TODAY, AND AN ESTIMATED 100 GALLONS HAS RELEASED SO FAR TODAY.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: 	CALLER REPORTING THE RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT (ESTIMATED TO BE MORE  THAT 1,000 GALLONS) OF SEWAGE ONTO THE ROAD, SOIL, AND INTO STORM DRAINS ON BASE. THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE IS UNKNOWN.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1463980 ///

/// THIS IS A 48 HOUR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1463979 ///

THE CALLER REPORTED THE FIRE HAS NOT YET BEEN EXTINGUISHED. NO OTHER MAJOR UPDATES AT THIS TIME.

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

THE CALLER IS REPORTING A RELEASE OF GASOLINE THAT CAUGHT FIRE ON A  TRANSMISSION PIPELINE. THE CALLER STATES CAUSE OF THE FIRE AND RELEASE OF  GASOLINE ARE UNKNOWN AT THIS TIME. CALLER STATES THAT MUHLENBERG COUNTY FIRST RESPONDERS PLACED A 0.5 MILE EVACUATION RADIUS IN THE AREA.

///UPDATE TO INCIDENT REPORT # 1463993///

UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: AFTER FURTHER INVESTIGATION WITH EPA WAS COMPLETED, THE CALLER STATES THE RELEASE IS FROM NATURAL SEEPAGE IN THE RIVER AND NOT FROM THEIR PIPELINES. 

ORIGINAL DESCRIPTION IS AS FOLLOWS: CALLER IS MAKING A REPORT INVOLVING A SPILL OF CRUDE OIL THAT WAS  DISCOVERED IN THE L.A. RIVER.  EXACT SOURCE OF THE CRUDE OIL IS UNKNOWN BUT THE CALLER STATES IT IS JUST NORTH OF THEIR LAST RELEASE FROM A PIPELINE AND SO THEY ARE MAKING THIS REPORT AS A PRECAUTION TO MAKE IT IS NOT ANOTHER SECTION OF THEIR PIPELINE THAT IT DISCHARGED FROM.  THE SHEEN  LENGTH IS AS FAR AS THE EYE CAN SEE.

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1463998///

UPDATED INFORMATION: THE AMOUNT OF MATERIAL THAT RELEASED WAS 400 GALLONS OF SOYBEAN OIL. 395 GALLONS WERE RECOVERED.

ORIGINAL REPORTED INFORMATION: THE CALLER IS REPORTING A RELEASE OF SOYBEAN OIL ONTO THE GROUND FROM A VAC TRUCK. THE CALLER STATES THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE WAS DUE TO THE HOSE CONNECTOR BREAKING ON A VAC TRUCK HOSE DURING AN ABOVE GROUND STORAGE TANK (#11) TO VAC TRUCK TRANSFER.

/// THIS IS ANOTHER UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1464028 ///

THE CALLER UPDATED THE RELEASE AMOUNT TO 180 GALLONS.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1464002 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THE AMOUNT OF PYGAS RELEASED IS NOW ESTIMATED TO BE 400  GALLONS.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS:  "PYGAS" RELEASED FROM A VACUUM BREAKER ON THE ROOF OF TANK 1701 DUE TO AN EQUIPMENT FAILURE.

/// THIS IS A CORRECTION TO NRC REPORT 1463906 /// 

THE CORRECTION IS AS FOLLOWS: THE INCIDENT LOCATION WAS LISTED AS ALBANY NEW YORK, HOWEVER THE ACTUAL LOCATION IS ALBANY KENTUCKY. THIS REPORT CORRECTS THIS ISSUE. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

THE CALLER STATED THAT A VESSEL WAS OVERFILLED DUE TO HEAT EXPANSION WHILE  IT WAS COVERED. BECAUSE OF THIS AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF GASOLINE RELEASED INTO LAKE CUMBERLAND. ALTHOUGH THE AMOUNT THAT RELEASED IS UNKNOWN THE CALLER  SUSPECTS LESS THAN (1) PINT.

/// NEEC INCIDENT NOTIFICATION: RED DOG ZINC SPILL WITH IMPACT TO RIVER |  COLUMBIA RIVER | TRAIL, BC SEA - DGIR 262004 ////

DESCRIPTION OF SPILL SITE AND SURROUNDING AREA:
KELOWNA FIRE RECEIVED A CALL FROM [THE SRP] REGARDING A DUMP TRUCK LOADED WITH RED DOG ZINC (HAZARDOUS MATERIAL) FOR THE LOCAL MINE 16KM AWAY.  MATERIAL WAS SPILLED TO HWY FOR 16KM.  SRP WAS UNSURE WHAT TO DO, AND REQUESTING GUIDANCE.  OO NOTED THE 16KM CROSSES A BRIDGE WITH PRECIPITATION EXPECTED THEREFORE EMAILING CCG.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1463746 ///

THE CALLER UPDATED THE RELEASE TO 400 POUNDS OF R449A REFRIGERANT. THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE WAS DUE TO A RUPTURED LINE ON RACK A. 1400 PEOPLE WERE EVACUATED. THE RELEASE HAS BEEN SECURED. REPAIRS ARE COMPLETED. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

